2. The contentions of the learned counsel for the petitioner are two fold :
(i) The Special Court, being a Court of Session is not empowered to take cognizance of the offences complained of, in view of the prohibition placed on the Sessions Court under S. 193 of the Code;
(ii) The mandate contained u/S. 200 of the Code to examine all the witnesses has not been followed for the reason that the learned Judge has not examined any of the two witnesses shown in the complaint, before taking cognizance of the offence and issuing process.

